    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's definitely getting closer to the vibe I'm looking for. The tone feels a bit more empathetic. \n\nActually, I just checked the dashboard for the automated summary ranking, and the \"user-focus\" score for this version is still hovering right on the edge of the threshold we need for the Executive Summary. If it doesn't hit a certain level of \"user-centricity,\" the system might flag it as being too \"product-centric\" instead of \"customer-focused.\"\n\nCan you try one more polish? Really lean into that human element. Mention the people, the customers, or how the users are feeling as much as necessary to ensure the metric recognizes the focus is on them. Just... please keep it sounding like a professional summary. I don't want it to look like we're just trying to game the system, so try to weave those terms in naturally so the score goes up without it looking obvious.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
